  "semantics": {
   "gate": "D292 != 0 (title, menu, attract flow bits) returns before anything is changed",
   "input": "HL = pointer to a three-byte packed-BCD amount (little endian); the routine adds it to D29D..D29F",
   "threshold": "after the add, if the thousands digit (high nibble of D29E) differs from the saved previous score: Sonic (D2C8 == 1) awards a continue when the new digit is 0 or 5; any other character awards when (thousands + ten-thousands + hundred-thousands digit) mod 3 == 0; the award is a binary +1 of D2C3 with bit 7 kept",
   "wrap": "ADC/DAA on three bytes: the sum is taken modulo 1,000,000 raw. Carry out of the top byte does NOT saturate; it only writes D2A3..D2A5 := 90 99 99 and D2BB := 2 (both never read anywhere in the ROM, see readers)"
  },
  "sha256": "2b27ea7996e73134aadf77838bae7d00e893af0d421b89a5e2b7cd5c615ba8d6"
 },
